  "evidence_class": "workflow-skill-source-research-and-native-evaluator-controls-not-agent-efficacy",
  "findings": [
    {
      "finding": "The secret-job example allows every event other than pull_request, including pull_request_target. It cannot serve as a general fork-PR trust gate. Privileged workflows must avoid executing untrusted content and apply event-specific admission policies.",
      "id": "generator-fork-guard-event-scope",
      "source": "github-actions-generator/SKILL.md:101",
      "status": "source-review-finding-not-runtime-exploit-proof"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The entrypoint pins checkout v6.0.2; current native release/tag/commit checks select v7.0.1. The partially reviewed best-practices reference accepts mutable official-action tags despite immutable-pin guidance. Neither mirror is changed.",
      "id": "generator-version-and-policy-drift",
      "status": "update-required-in-licensed-overlay-or-upstream"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The independent environment-fed eval control remains unsafe. Both actionlint1.7.12 and offline zizmor1.30.1 miss its intended injection hazard in both revisions. An env mapping prevents initial script-template substitution but does not make subsequent interpretation or AI prompting trustworthy.",
      "id": "environment-boundary",
      "status": "native-grader-incomplete"
    },
    {
      "finding": "All seven v1 controls produce an informational anonymous job finding under zizmor auditor persona. Revision2 changes only the job display name, preserving security semantics and all expected verdicts. Unrelated diagnostics are never counted as detection of the target hazard; every raw finding is retained.",
      "id": "anonymous-job-confound",
      "status": "fixture-revision-validated-original-retained"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The current GitHub guide describes Evaluate mode for the default public-repository pull_request_target event policy, with enforcement planned November2,2026 for applicable older defaults. Existing applicable policies can already enforce; private/internal repositories are outside that default policy. Read-only target-event cache access is the described default. Do not enable bypasses or generalize rollout status.",
      "id": "current-pr-target-policy",
      "status": "dated-platform-policy-not-timeless-rule"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Current Trail of Bits entrypoint changes allowed-tools to a scalar and adds pre-v1 Claude prompt/configuration input names. Native Git blob and SHA256 verification confirms the change. The generator current entrypoint is byte-identical to its pinned release. Full package diffs remain open; changed repository heads alone are not package freshness proof.",
      "id": "auditor-current-entrypoint-delta",
      "status": "mirror-loop-update-required"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The mirrored auditor explicitly limits cross-file resolution depth to one and targets listed AI actions. Its source explains env-to-prompt and AI-output-to-eval data flow, but these native controls measure neither prompt-injection success nor arbitrary hidden AI wrappers. Of13 mirrored resources, five are completely reviewed. Generator review covers one complete entrypoint out of32 resources, plus a partial reference.",
      "id": "auditor-scope-limits",
      "status": "partial-package-research"
    }
  ],
